############### -----GNIRS NORTH----- ####################
#	    			   Build Instructions                     #
#																			#
#																			#
#  The following instuction should be followed to setup  #
#  and build GNIRS at Gemini North 		                  #
##########################################################

1. This current directory is GNIRS_TOP. It contains the
   GNIRS_TOP version of nirs.env and should be modified
	to reflect key environment variables for the build.

   !!!!However!!!! Please note that subsystems (when built)
	will NOT put install files into this level of the GNIRS
	tree.

2. Scripts are never executed from the GNIRS_TOP directory.

3. Subsystem dircectories such as CC, DC, IS also include files
	called nirs.env. These 'sub' versions of nirs.env only
	call the GNIRS_TOP level of nirs.env with the specific
	subsystem name such as CC, DC, IS, passed as an argument to
	the local nirsSetup script.

4. -------OK. Get on with the build!--------
   a. Edit $GNIRS_TOP/nirs.env to change the NIRS_DIR line
	to equal the full path of your current GNIRS_TOP directory.
	Using ${PWD} may get you into trouble.

5. Build CC
   a. cd to CC

   a.1. check nirs.env for anything odd.

   a.2. Run 'nirs.env'

   b. Watch if applSetup ran correctly

   c. Check that config/CONFIG.Defs contains the proper setting
      for APPLIC_IOCPATH. It should be set to
      pisces:/gemini/GEM5/gnirs/CC/<NIRS_CVSRELEASE>. Be carefull
      because this is the path that gets installed and can wipe out
      your existing deployed build.

   c.1. Run gmake.

   d. Check for presence of Distfile. Remember you're still
      in the CC dir. If Distfile does not exist run gmake Distfile.
      This will create your local CC Distfile. Check that it looks OK
      and will ******NOT****** over write something in /gemini/GEM5 or
      otherwise do something you don't expect!

   d.1. Solaris directory not automatically made. Do a,
        "mkdir bin/solaris".

   e. gmake rdist installs CC into correct location

6. Build IS

   a. cd to IS

   a.1. edit nirs.env and change (or add) NIRS_CVSRELEASE to the IS
        specific CVS release tag. NIRS_CVSRELEASE is used to create
        the path to install in, so something like, "V1-2TEST" is
        a good idea for your initial run.

   a.2. Run 'nirs.env'

   b. Watch if applSetup ran correctly

   c. Check that config/CONFIG.DEF contains the proper setting
      for APPLIC_IOCPATH. It should be set to
      pisces:/gemini/GEM5/gnirs/IS/<NIRS_CVSRELEASE>. If there is
      a problem try, "rm -rf config" and re-run nirs.env.
 
   c.1. Run gmake.

   d. Check for presence of Distfile. Remember you're still
      in the IS dir. If Distfile does not exist run "gmake Distfile".
      This will create your local IS Distfile.  Check that it looks OK
      and will ** NOT ** over write something in /gemini/GEM5 or
      otherwise do something you don't expect!

   e. gmake rdist installs IS into correct location

****************** Don't bother with WFS  - not commisioned! *****************
7. Build WFS (This one has 3 TOP levels!)
	a. cd to WFS dir and edit 'nirsLogin' to reflect your local build environment.
		This is the WFS_TOP directory setup file. Adjust the CVS_RELEASE keyword to
		a tag that's convenient for you.
	
	b. cd to ENG and type ./nirsSetup. This is the ENG TOP build.

   c. Check that applSetup ran correctly.

   d. Check that config/CONFIG.DEF contains the proper setting
		for APPLIC_IOCPATH. It should be set to 
		pisces:/gemini/GEM5/gnirs/WFS/WFS/ENG/<CVS_RELEASE>

   d. Check for presence of Distfile. Remember you're still
		in the WFS/ENG dir. If Distfile does not exist run gmake Distfile.
		This will create your local IS Distfile. Check that it
		looks OK and will ******NOT****** over write something
		in /gemini/GEM5 or otherwise do something you don't expect!

	e. Change to WFS/LIB and WFS/WFS (yes 2 deep) and repeat the above 
		steps to procuce all binaries in the three directories.

	f. As an example of a correct looking install see: /gemini/GEM5/gnirs/WFS/...

****************** NOW DC1 ***************

8. Build DC (THis has the DHS client ppc(GEM7) directory embedded in the
	EPICS DC_TOP(GEM5) directory).

	a. cd to DC/ppc and check the environment variable are set in epicsGEM7.cshrc, 
		including NIRS_CVSRELEASE tag name.

	b. source $GEM7 environment

	c. run nirs.env and check that applSetup executed correcly

	d. Again check that APPLIC_IOCPATH looks good. Something like 
		pisces:/gemini/epics3.13.4/gnirs/DC/<NIRS_CVSRELEASE>/ppc 

	e. Check that Distfile looks correct.

	g. gmake rdist as gemvx

9. Jump up one level now to the DC_TOP for the DC2 EPICS build.
	
	a. Checking that the GNIRS_TOP/nirs.env has all the correct environment vars,
		proceed to 'source $GEM5', and run the local nirs.env.

	b. Check that config/CONFIG.DEF contains the proper setting
		for APPLIC_IOCPATH. It should be set to something like 
		pisces:/gemini/GEM5/gnirs/DC/<CVS_RELEASE>. 
		NOTE that the current configuration puts both DC builds (EPICS and DHS )
		into /gemini/epics3.13.4/gnirs/gnirs.fkraemer.test/DC/ and .../DC/ppc
		respectively.

	c. Check that Distfile looks correct.

        c.1 Make the following directries b/c they are not created automatically:
           mkdir bin/solaris
           mkdir lib
           mkdir include
           mkdir dbd

	d. gmake rdist


# 10. Now there should be quite a few symbolic links in the install trees to change.

 

IF one of [CC DC IS WFS] is sent as a parameter to nirs.env just that area will
setup.  


To start the dm screens run "nirsSeqStart".  This sets some environment 
variables and runs dm with the correct parameters.  

